# cavekit-find-on-page.md R1 (T-678): Find on Page works on the browser's own pages as on a web page: about:settings
# ("personas": its Browser tab's first section and row) and about:data ("site data", its heading), found and counted.
id: find-own-pages
section: Find on page
item: Find on Page on the browser's own pages: "personas" on about:settings and "site data" on about:data are found and counted
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: about:settings
kit: cavekit-find-on-page.md R1
wait rect page-title 20
sample before-menu 0,30,300,180
chrome appmenu
wait differs 0,30,300,180 before-menu 5
wait still 0,30,300,180 3
mark
chrome appmenu-find
expect keyboard up 8
type-keys personas
wait line 'find .8 bytes. -> 1' 10
wait line 'find-result: {"index":[1-9][0-9]*,"total":[1-9]' 10
mark
chrome find-done
wait line 'find: cleared' 8
launch about:data
wait rect page-title 20
sample before-menu2 0,30,300,180
chrome appmenu
wait differs 0,30,300,180 before-menu2 5
wait still 0,30,300,180 3
mark
chrome appmenu-find
expect keyboard up 8
type-keys site data
wait line 'find .9 bytes. -> 1' 10
wait line 'find-result: {"index":[1-9][0-9]*,"total":[1-9]' 10
shoot own-page
mark
chrome find-done
wait line 'find: cleared' 8
